go: give each package's cgo output directory a path of its own.

cgo writes a package's generated files into one directory, cgo_gen_tmp,
and cxx names each C compile action after its source's path, so the
generated _cgo_export.c compiled as "c_compile cgo_gen_tmp/_cgo_export.c"
in every cgo package. go_stdlib builds the whole standard library in one
target (prelude//go/tools:stdlib), and four of its packages use cgo
(runtime/cgo, plugin, net/internal/cgotest, internal/runtime/cgobench),
so four actions of that target had the same category and identifier.

buck2 requires category and identifier to be unique for a target, and
keys its local action cache (the in-memory dep-file state) by exactly
that. The four compiles overwrote each other's entry. Whenever the
daemon dropped DICE but kept that state (the notify watcher reporting
dropped events), each compile found another package's entry or none,
and ran again with an unchanged command line.

The directory cgo writes into is now cgo_gen_pkg/<import path>
(cgo_gen_pkg for a package at the root of a cell, whose import path is
empty), so the identifier is "cgo_gen_pkg/<import path>/_cgo_export.c".
It is deliberately not under cgo_gen_tmp: content-based paths give the
old and the new directory the same hash prefix, and in a buck-out that
still held the old directory, an output nested inside it came out empty.
The deeper directory leaves source positions alone: before Go 1.27 cgo's
//line paths are trimmed to the project root, and from 1.27 they are
relative to this directory, which the Go compiler resolves them against.
A package without cgo files still gets an empty cgo_gen_tmp: nothing is
compiled out of it, so its name doesn't matter.

--- a/go/cgo_builder.bzl
+++ b/go/cgo_builder.bzl
@@ -96,7 +96,14 @@
     """
     Run `cgo` on `.go` sources to generate Go, C, and C-Header sources.
     """
-    gen_dir = actions.declare_output("cgo_gen_tmp", dir = True, has_content_based_path = True)
+    # cxx names each C compile action after its source's path, and buck2 needs
+    # action identifiers unique within a target. go_stdlib builds every
+    # standard package in one target, so the path holds the import path (empty
+    # for a package at the root of the cell). It is not under "cgo_gen_tmp",
+    # which an older buck-out may still hold: an output nested in another
+    # output's directory there comes out empty.
+    gen_dir_path = paths.join("cgo_gen_pkg", pkg_import_path) if pkg_import_path else "cgo_gen_pkg"
+    gen_dir = actions.declare_output(gen_dir_path, dir = True, has_content_based_path = True)
 
     # Return a `cmd_args` to use as the generated sources.
 
